  "worked_solution": "A function $f(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={f}^{\u2033}(x),$ we can see that ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ on the intervals  $(0,1)$ and  $(1,2).$  Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is concave up on the intervals\n\n$$\n(\\,0,1\\,)\\,\\text{and}\\,(\\,1,2\\,).\n$$",
